WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.773
The robot's policy never changes.

2
00:00:02.773 --> 00:00:06.259
An engineering agent improves the
installation around it.

3
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:12.262
First job: the bowl on the cabinet and the
middle drawer open, together,

4
00:00:12.262 --> 00:00:14.842
on at least 18 of 20 fresh starts.

5
00:00:14.842 --> 00:00:17.535
The robot has a skill for each half.

6
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.471
Chained plainly, the hand turns to the
drawer still touching the bowl,

7
00:00:23.471 --> 00:00:25.161
and knocks it off.

8
00:00:25.161 --> 00:00:28.092
On the agent's practice starts: 5 of 10.

9
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.001
The agent writes a check: does the bowl
stay in place while the next skill runs?

10
00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.924
Then it changes one thing at a time.

11
00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:40.359
Open, then go home: 5 of 10.

12
00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:44.864
Let the placement run 30 steps longer,
then go home: 10 of 10.

13
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:51.435
Confirmed 20 of 20 on unused starts, then
20 of 20 reserved starts,

14
00:00:51.435 --> 00:00:55.717
against 1 for the plain chain: 19 rescued,
0 broken.

15
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.665
It keeps the job, the check, and a lesson:
an open,

16
00:01:04.665 --> 00:01:09.388
still hand at one instant has not cleared
the path that follows.

17
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.277
Second job: the plate at the front of the
stove and the bowl on the cabinet.

18
00:01:15.277 --> 00:01:17.202
Again, at least 18 of 20.

19
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.124
Plate first, then bowl: 7 of 10 practice
starts.

20
00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:26.948
Here the plate push runs out of time short
of the stove.

21
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:32.918
The agent extends the first job's check to
both goals and tests changes.

22
00:01:32.918 --> 00:01:36.085
Going home between skills: 8 of 10
delivered.

23
00:01:36.085 --> 00:01:40.253
Loading the cheese into the bowl gets
every plate to the stove,

24
00:01:40.253 --> 00:01:44.365
but the loaded bowl becomes the
bottleneck: 4 of 10 delivered.

25
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:52.476
So the agent grasps the cheese, slides it
aside onto the table,

26
00:01:52.476 --> 00:01:55.898
and leaves the bowl empty: 10 of 10
delivered.

27
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:05.165
Confirmed 20 of 20 on unused starts, then
20 of 20 reserved starts,

28
00:02:05.165 --> 00:02:08.985
against 5 for the plain chain: 15 rescued,
0 broken.

29
00:02:08.985 --> 00:02:12.028
Here the plain chain reaches the stove,

30
00:02:12.028 --> 00:02:15.729
but its bowl attempt leaves neither goal
standing.

31
00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.211
It keeps the job, the extended check, and
a lesson:

32
00:02:20.211 --> 00:02:23.923
preparing the scene can move the
bottleneck to the next skill.

33
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.330
Story two: a fleet of arms at several
sites,

34
00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:32.187
with the same lag at one site and on one
robot elsewhere.

35
00:02:32.187 --> 00:02:36.155
The agent builds its own probe, commanded
against measured:

36
00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:40.850
one lag is a fixed network delay, the
other a controller falling behind.

37
00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:47.115
After paired experiments it compensates
for the delay,

38
00:02:47.115 --> 00:02:51.704
rolls back an update and services the
controller.

39
00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:57.797
On 576 reserved attempts it never saw,
success rises from 451 to 558:

40
00:02:57.797 --> 00:03:00.354
113 rescued, 6 broken.

41
00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.677
Two jobs at 20 and 20 of 20 reserved
starts,

42
00:03:04.677 --> 00:03:08.245
and a fleet improved by an instrument the
agent built.

43
00:03:08.245 --> 00:03:11.867
The policy never changed; every clip is a
recorded run.
